---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: portable-app-lifecycle-contract
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  Client-facing portable app lifecycle contracts. Runtime adapters own effects and authority;
  generic demand leases live in the lower-level seam-contracts crate. These interfaces do not
  implement a process supervisor, session channel, replica store or authentication portal.
---

Source vocabulary comes from SDK schemas; shared Rust views generate client types. Passing-state
sessions belong to the live-session work, not this module. Observation persistence reuses the
existing observation intent and receipt, retaining signed=absent/as-asserted until actual proof.
No successful no-op defaults: missing adapters report Unsupported. Contracts are not delivery.

The owning roadmap is `genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-14-portable-app-lifecycle-design.md`.
The native gate is `just gate elohim-sdk`; views use `just gate app-lifecycle-contracts`.
